/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 121 0 R
/T (In rain[i][j], i is the district \(row\) and j is the month \(column\). C stores a 2-D array row by row, so rain[i][j] sits right next to rain[i][j+1]. Address = base + \(i x 12 + j\) x size. Going row-wise reads neighbouring memory \(fast, cache friendly\); going column-wise jumps 12 elements each step \(slower\).)
/E (In rain[i][j], i is the district \(row\) and j is the month \(column\). C stores a 2-D array row by row, so rain[i][j] sits right next to rain[i][j+1]. Address = base + \(i x 12 + j\) x size. Going row-wise reads neighbouring memory \(fast, cache friendly\); going column-wise jumps 12 elements each step \(slower\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
