/T (isspace\(\) treats a tab as a separator, so "Hello\\tWorld" gives 2 words. A version that tests only for ' ' would count 1. Safety: strcpy does not check the size of the destination, so a long text copied into a small array overflows it; use strncpy/snprintf and fgets. gets\(\) was removed from C11 for the same reason.)
/E (isspace\(\) treats a tab as a separator, so "Hello\\tWorld" gives 2 words. A version that tests only for ' ' would count 1. Safety: strcpy does not check the size of the destination, so a long text copied into a small array overflows it; use strncpy/snprintf and fgets. gets\(\) was removed from C11 for the same reason.)
